{
  "requirement": "Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests\nseparately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.doctests` has one MUST. Habeas's bundled agent instructions must direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`. The requirement text carries `:impl: agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`. The bundled instructions are therefore the skills under `assets/skills` and the SOP.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` carries a `{test}` reference to the subject. It checks the obligation for each instruction document that states the direction:\n- **Skill loop.** For `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, it asserts that the collapsed bundled skill text (including reference files) contains `` `cargo test --doc --workspace` ``.\n- **Home skill.** For `habeas`, `assert_text` requires the phrase \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n- **Other two skills.** For `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `assert_text` requires \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n- **SOP.** For `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`, loaded with `include_str!`, `assert_text` requires \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n\nThe tests assert on the actual shipped files. The matches I found are the SOP, `habeas/SKILL.md`, `habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`. Removing or rewording the direction in any of them fails the test. This includes dropping \"separately\" or changing the command, because the assertions match the full phrases.\n\n**Scope.** The test does not check `habeas-refactor`, `habeas-requirements` or the other SOPs. The requirement does not say every instruction file must carry the direction. The `:impl:` anchor names the approved-implementation SOP as the implementing instruction, and the skills that handle coverage and testing are covered as well. I do not treat the uncovered files as a gap.\n\n**Other checks.**\n- The requirement has no boundary or failure cases beyond the presence of this direction.\n- The `GUIDANCE` string in `src/execution_coverage.rs` is CLI output, not bundled agent instructions, so it needs no test here.\n- There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and I found no gap.",
  "references": "0fe66373f599880ea97b9de591948b4d4a6a583dd2b16af10dccdfce984d9839",
